    - governance  # 0238
    before: []  # 0238
    duplicate_of: []  # 0238
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 0238
    pr_ref:  # 0238
    description: "**Per `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bf4oxh91w_investigation_threads_04072026_1702.md` Thread 8 §\"Proposed fixes\" rank #3:** when the stop hook fires, if an active background task launched by the current session exists, the guidance text should explicitly say:\n\n> You have an active background task `<id>` running command `<cmd>`. Do not start anything that could conflict with it. Wait for the notification or check liveness with `TaskList` — do not infer task state from stdout files.\n\n**Why:** root cause analysis of the bf4oxh91w incident (see companion invariant item) identified stop-hook anxiety as the primary causal factor: 54 seconds between stop-hook fire (L253, 19:31:25) and the destructive duplicate-launch (L263, 19:32:19), under \"TODOs are blocking\" pressure. The companion smart-test flock fix makes the *specific* failure mode (duplicate `smart-test`) structurally impossible, but does NOT address the more general failure mode where the agent takes premature action on any other long-running command under stop-hook pressure.\n\n**Implementation surface:** stop hook guidance generation in `.agent/hooks/`. Would need to:\n1. Detect active background tasks for the current session — likely via the harness's `TaskList` mechanism, or by reading task output directories under `/tmp/claude-<uid>/.../tasks/`.\n2. Inject task-aware text into the stop guidance file (which is what the hook returns to the harness for the next prompt).\n3. Suppress or soften the \"TODOs blocking\" framing while a long-running background task is in flight, since the agent's correct response is \"wait\" not \"drive forward.\"\n\n**STATUS: needs_human_review per AGENTS.md governance file list. `.agent/hooks/` is governance.**\n\n**Approval workflow:** this item stays in `needs_human_review` until the human approves the design. After approval, an implementation item touching `.agent/hooks/` can be created and submitted as a PR with explicit authorization.\n\n**Pairs with:**\n- The smart-test flock fix (immediate structural fix for the most common case)\n- The companion invariant item documenting the violation\n- AGENTS.md/playbook additions about TaskList habituation (also governance)\n\n**Open question worth flagging during human review:** how does the hook know which background tasks belong to the *current* session vs others? The harness's task ID space may not be session-scoped. If not, the detection has to fall back to \"any background task on the system from this user\" which has false positives. Worth resolving before implementation."  # 0238
    fields: {}  # 0238
